==Hungarian==

===Etymology===
{{doublet|hu|és|t1=and}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{hu-IPA}}
* {{audio|hu|Hu-is.ogg}}
* {{rhymes|hu|iʃ|s=1}}

===Adverb===
{{hu-adv|-}} {{tlb|hu|clitic}}{{cln|hu|clitics}}<!-- https://www.nyest.hu/hirek/a-kottazo-gorogok "A magyarban simulószó például az is, az -e és a névelők. Ezt néha egybeírás is jelöli: úgyis, máris, néha viszont nem: végül is." -->

# [[also]], [[too]], [[as well]]
#: {{syn|hu|szintén|ugyancsak|úgyszintén|éppúgy|szintúgy|q5=formal; the others are relatively literary in style}}
#: {{uxi|hu|Én '''is''' szeretem a csokit.|I, '''too,''' like chocolate (aside from other people).}}
#: {{uxi|hu|(Én) a csokit '''is''' szeretem.|I '''also''' like chocolate (aside from other things).}} <!-- "also" normally refers to the object -->
# [[even]], [[up to]], [[as much as]], [[as long as]]
#: {{uxi|hu|Három óráig '''is''' tarthat a műtét|The operation may '''even''' take three hours.}}
# {{lb|hu|after an interrogative word}} [[again]] {{gloss|used in a question to ask something one has forgotten}}
#: {{uxi|hu|Hogy '''is''' hívják?|What's that called, '''again'''?}}
## {{lb|hu|in a rhetorical question}} [[ever]] {{gloss|intensifying the question}}
##: {{uxi|hu|Hogy '''is''' felejthetném el?|How could I '''ever''' forget?}}
##: {{uxi|hu|Miért '''is''' nem maradtam otthon?|Why, '''oh why''' did I not stay home?}}
# [[sure enough]], [[indeed]]
#: {{syn|hu|tényleg|valóban|csakugyan}}
#: {{uxi|hu|Aznapra esőt mondtak, és el '''is''' kezdett esni.|Rain had been predicted for that day and, '''sure enough''', it was beginning to rain.|lit=They had said rain for…}}

====Usage notes====
When it is used with a [[concessive]] adverb (“no matter what/​who​/​when/how”, “however [good, bad]”, “long as it was”, “even if…” etc.), it is traditionally placed after the verb, though it is common in colloquial style to use it after the adverb instead:
: {{ux|hu|''(traditionally, chiefly in literary style)'' Bármilyen hosszúra nyúlt '''is''' az előadás,…<br/>''(more recently)'' Bármilyen hosszúra '''is''' nyúlt az előadás,…|No matter how long the lecture​/​performance stretched,…}}
It applies to [[Appendix:Hungarian verb-final set phrases|verb-final set phrases]] as well, similarly to {{m|hu|érez|érzi magát}} in this clause: {{m|hu||még ha ettől rosszul érezzük '''is''' magunkat / …rosszul '''is''' érezzük magunkat|even if it makes us feel bad}}.<!-- in the original, of which it is not a literal translation: "no matter how queasy it
makes us feel" -->

Questions that have an "is" standing after an interrogative word (in sense 3) are spoken with a rising intonation which then falls on the last syllable – like yes-or-no questions –, in contrast with those without "is", which have falling intonation throughout the sentence. Rhetorical questions (sense 3.1) don't have this distinction.

